* The ⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000001⟫

This tour is built atop the [[⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000002⟫][⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000003⟫]], a
web service that runs on [[⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000004⟫][golang.org]]'s servers.

The service receives a ⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000005⟫ program, compiles, links, and runs the program inside
a sandbox, then returns the output.

There are limitations to the programs that can be run in the ⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000006⟫:

- In the ⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000007⟫ the time begins at 2009-11-10 23:00:00 ⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000008⟫ (determining the significance of this date is an exercise for the reader). This makes it easier to cache programs by giving them deterministic output.

- There are also limits on execution time and on ⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000009⟫ and memory usage, and the program cannot access external network hosts.

The ⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000010⟫ uses the latest stable release of ⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000011⟫.

Read "[[⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000012⟫][Inside the ⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000013⟫]]" to learn more.

⟪GTI18N_19e6d7da_000014⟫
